This research prototype uses the existing ordinary undirected Curveball
algorithm through NetworKit 11.2.2, a separately installed dependency.
No NetworKit, Python, NumPy, SciPy, psutil, NetworkX, tabulate, setuptools,
or other third-party runtime binaries are distributed in this source release
or in this package's pure-Python wheel.

Algorithm attribution:
Carstens, Berger and Strona, arXiv:1609.05137v3.
Carstens et al., arXiv:1804.08487v2, ESA 2018.
Dyer, Greenhill and Ullrich, arXiv:1301.4055.
Related fixed-margin binary-matrix theory:
Fu, Qin and Wang, arXiv:2606.22636v2.

The conditional undirected operator input is OpenAI/math family 131,
commit fd4aeeb2ee4fc729c18d98444fed42fd0529eeeb.
The ordinary-Curveball corollary and this software are distinct from
the source manuscript's switch-chain comparison and from any simplex
projection-volume result.

